libdoom-umapinfo: Update to 2.0.0

2.0.0  2026-10-24  Release
--------------------------

Fixed:
- Correctly map first octet of quoted string to '?' (if it is not a
  printable US-ASCII character) for terminal output of command line
  utility

Changed:
- Breaking: New major version (not ABI compatible with major version 1)
- Breaking: Change path of header file
- Breaking: Change API namespace prefix
- Breaking: Rename command line utility to "doom-umapinfo2-cli"
- Accept data conforming to UMAPINFO Rev 2.3
  Update syntax definition (file "SYNTAX")
- Replace license CC0 1.0 Universal (SPDX ID "CC0-1.0")
  with BSD Zero Clause License (SPDX ID "0BSD")
- Testsuite requires POSIX.1-2001
- Color output for rule "test" to run testsuite with POSIX make

Added:
- Guide for update from major version 1 (file "MIGRATION")
- Dual license option for code
  - BSD 2-Clause "Simplified" License
  - GNU General Public License v2.0 or later
  (SPDX license-expression "BSD-2-Clause OR GPL-2.0-or-later")
- Keywords "jumping", "crouching" and "freeaim"
- Ternary identifiers "disallow", "allow" and "require"
- Support for port-exclusive keywords and identifiers
- Rule "check" to run testsuite with POSIX make
  For compatibility with GNU autotools
- Rule "test-mono" to run testsuite with POSIX make
  and monochrome output (color is the default)
- More unit tests
